"GitHub - deepglint/DanQing: The official repo for the DanQing dataset. · GitHub (https://github.com/deepglint/DanQing)\nciteturn30924view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn30923view2\",\"lineno\":220}); Total lines: 371\nL180:   * cite86†💡 Highlights L181:   * cite87†💻 Dataset Information L182:     * cite88†Data Preview L183:     * cite89†Topic Assessment L184:     * cite90†Image Resolution and Text Length Distribution L185:     * cite91†Text Quality L186:     * cite92†Cosine Similarity and Semantic Distribution L187:   * cite93†📊 Performance Comparison L188:     * cite94†Zero-Shot Classification L189:     * cite95†Cross-Modal Retrieval (Short Caption) L190:     * cite96†Cross-Modal Retrieval (Long Caption) L191:     * cite97†Chinese-Centric Large Multimodal Model Tasks L192:   * cite98†🧠 Analysis L193:     * cite99†Data and Model Scaling L194:     * cite100†New Concept Understanding L195:   * cite101†📥 Download L196:     * cite102†🤗 Hugging Face L197:       * cite103†Python API L198:       * cite104†Command Line L199:     * cite105†ModelScope L200:       * cite106†Python API L201:       * cite107†Command Line L202:   * cite108†📄 License L203:   * cite109†📝 Citation L204: * * *\nL205: ## 💡 Highlights\nL206: \nL207: In this paper, we propose DanQing dataset, which contains 100 million image-text pairs collected from Common Crawl. Different from existing datasets, DanQing is curated through a more rigorous selection process, yielding superior data quality. Moreover, DanQing is primarily built from 2024–2025 web data, enabling models to better capture evolving semantic trends and thus offering greater practical utility.\nL208: We compare DanQing with existing datasets by conducting continual pre-training of the SigLIP2 model. Experimental results show that DanQing consistently achieves superior performance across a range of Chinese downstream tasks, including zero-shot classification, cross-modal retrieval, and LMM-based evaluations.\nL209: \nL210: * * *\nL211: ## 💻 Dataset Information\nL212: \nL213: ### Data Preview\nL214: ### Topic Assessment\nL215: \nL216: We implement a topic modeling pipeline based on cite110†BERTopic . We randomly sample 10M image-text pairs and extract text embeddings using cite111†Chinese-CLIP-L/14 . To address high-dimensional clustering, we apply UMAP for dimensionality reduction, followed by HDBSCAN to identify semantic clusters with a minimum cluster size of 1,000 for stability and noise reduction. Finally, we use class-based TF-IDF to extract representative keywords for each topic.\nL217: ### Image Resolution and Text Length Distribution\nL218: \nL219: We analyze image resolutions by width, height, and minimum dimension, demonstrating a wide range of visual scales. We also report the distribution of text lengths across 2.2B Chinese words.\nL220: ### Text Quality\nL221: \nL222: We evaluate the text quality of DanQing using two metrics: semantic word density and perplexity (PPL). We randomly sample 10M texts from DanQing, Wukong, and Zero for comparison. Semantic words (nouns, verbs, adjectives) are identified using the jieba toolkit, and their proportion in each sentence is calculated as semantic density. Sentence-level perplexity is computed with a pre-trained Chinese cite112†BERT†huggingface.co model.\nL223: ### Cosine Similarity and Semantic Distribution\nL224: \nL225: We analyze 10M-sample subsets of DanQing and Wukong by presenting image-text similarity distributions, extracted with cite113†FG-CLIP2-L/16@256†huggingface.co . For semantic distribution comparison, 10M images from each dataset are clustered into 10K groups using cite114†FAISS , with clusters ranked by sample count.\nL226: \nL227: * * *\nL228: \nL229: ## 📊 Performance Comparison\nL230: \nL231: ### Zero-Shot Classification\nL232: \nL233: ### Cross-Modal Retrieval (Short Caption)\nL234: ### Cross-Modal Retrieval (Long Caption)\nL235: \nL236: ### Chinese-Centric Large Multimodal Model Tasks\nL237: \nL238: * * *\nL239: \nL240: ## 🧠 Analysis\nL241: \nL242: ### Data and Model Scaling\nL243: \nL244: We compare the data and model scaling capabilities of DanQing and Wukong, reporting average zero-shot classification and retrieval (long & short caption) performance in the figure below.\nL245: ### New Concept Understanding\nL246: \nL247: We evaluate SigLIP2-L/16 models pre-trained on various Chinese datasets for emergent concept understanding, and find that the model trained on DanQing consistently gives the highest confidence to correct pairs.\nL248: \nL249: * * *\nL250: \nL251: ## 📥 Download\nL252: \nL253: ### 🤗 Hugging Face\nL254: \nL255: #### Python API\nL256: \nL257:     from datasets import load_dataset\nL258: \nL259:     ds = load_dataset(\"DeepGlint-AI/DanQing100M\")\nL260: #### Command Line\nL261: \nL262:     # Install dependencies\nL263:     # brew install git-xet  # macOS\nL264:     # git xet install\nL265: \nL266:     # sudo apt update  # Ubuntu/Debian\nL267:     # sudo apt install aria2\nL268: \nL269:     # Install git-lfs\nL270:     # curl -s https://packagecloud.io/install/repositories/github/git-lfs/script.deb.sh | sudo bash\nL271:     # sudo apt-get install git-lfs\nL272:     # git lfs install\nL273: \nL274:     # Download dataset URLs and captions\nL275:     bash hfd.sh DeepGlint-AI/DanQing100M --dataset --tool aria2c -x 10\nL276:     # Download images using img2dataset\nL277:     # pip install img2dataset\nL278:     # For better performance, it's highly recommended to set up a fast dns resolver\nL279:     # See: https://github.com/rom1504/img2dataset#setting-up-a-high-performance-dns-resolver\nL280:     img2dataset --url_list DanQing100M/data \\\nL281:             --input_format \"parquet\" \\\nL282:             --url_col \"url\" \\\nL283:             --caption_col \"alt_text\" \\\nL284:             --output_format webdataset \\\nL285:             --output_folder DanQing100M-webdataset \\\nL286:             --processes_count 16 \\\nL287:             --thread_count 32 \\\nL288:             --image_size 256 \\\nL289:             --resize_only_if_bigger=True \\\nL290:             --resize_mode=\"keep_ratio\" \\\nL291:             --skip_reencode=True \\\nL292:             --save_additional_columns '[\"recaption\"]' \\\nL293:             --enable_wandb False\nL294: ### ModelScope\nL295: \nL296: #### Python API\nL297: \nL298:     from modelscope.msdatasets import MsDataset\nL299: \nL300:     ds = MsDataset.load('deepglint/DanQing')\nL301: #### Command Line\nL302: \nL303:     pip install modelscope\nL304: \nL305:     # ref: https://modelscope.cn/docs/datasets/download\nL306:     # Application approved instantly\nL307:     export YOUR_MODELSCOPE_ACCESS_TOKEN=''\nL308:     export LOCAL_DIR=''\nL309:     modelscope login --token $YOUR_MODELSCOPE_ACCESS_TOKEN\nL310:     modelscope --token $YOUR_MODELSCOPE_ACCESS_TOKEN download --dataset deepglint/DanQing --local_dir $LOCAL_DIR\nL311: \nL312: * * *\nL313: ## 📄 License\nL314: \nL315: The DanQing dataset is licensed under CC-BY-NC-4.0 License. The dataset is collected from Common Crawl web pages and may contain biased or sensitive content. The collected data is subject to the license to which each content belongs. Users are solely responsible for ensuring compliance with ethical and legal standards in their research or applications.\nL316: \nL317: * * *\nL318: ## 📝 Citation\nL319: If you find this repository useful, please use the following BibTeX entry for citation.\nL320: \nL321:     @misc{danqing,\nL322:           title={DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset},\nL323:           author={Hengyu Shen and Tiancheng Gu and Bin Qin and Lan Wu and Yuling Wu and Shuo Tan and Zelong Sun and Jun Wang and Nan Wu and Xiang An and Weidong Cai and Ziyong Feng and Kaicheng Yang},\nL324:           year={2026},\nL325:           eprint={2601.10305},\nL326:           archivePrefix={arXiv},\nL327:           primaryClass={cs.CV},\nL328:           url={https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10305},\nL329:     }\nL330: * * *\nL331: ### ⭐ Don't forget to star this repository if you find it helpful!\nL332: \nL333: ## About\nL334: \nL335: The official repo for the DanQing dataset.\nL336: \nL337: cite115†deepglint.github.io/DanQing/†deepglint.github.io L338: \nL339: ### Topics\nL340: \nL341: cite116†chinese-clip cite117†chinese-dataset cite118†clip cite119†large-scale-image-text-dataset cite120†multimodal-representation-learning cite121†vision-language-model L342: \nL343: ### Resources\nL344: \nL345: cite122†Readme L346: \nL347: cite123†CC-BY-4.0 license L348: \nL349: cite124†Activity L350: \nL351: cite125†Custom properties L352: \nL353: ### Stars\nL354: \nL355: 39 stars\nL356: \nL357: ### Watchers\nL358: \nL359: 0 watching\nL360: ### Forks\nL361: \nL362: cite126†0 forks L363: \nL364: cite127†Report repository L365: \nL366: ## Contributors\nL367: \nL368: ## Languages\nL369: \nL370: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2601.10305] DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset (https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.10305)\nciteturn30924view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"turn30923view3\",\"lineno\":12}); Total lines: 164\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Jan 2026 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 25 Mar 2026 (this version, v3)]\nL9: # Title:DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Hengyu Shen , cite7†Tiancheng Gu , cite8†Bin Qin , cite9†Lan Wu , cite10†Yuling Wu , cite11†Shuo Tan , cite12†Zelong Sun , cite13†Jun Wang , cite14†Nan Wu , cite15†Xiang An , cite16†Weidong Cai , cite17†Ziyong Feng , cite18†Kaicheng Yang L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset, by Hengyu Shen and 12 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite19†View PDF cite20†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Vision-Language Pre-training (VLP) models have achieved remarkable success by leveraging large-scale image-text pairs. While English-centric models like CLIP and SigLIP benefit from massive datasets (e.g., LAION-400M), the development of Chinese VLP remains bottlenecked by the lack of high-quality, large-scale open-source data. In this paper, we present DanQing, a large-scale Chinese cross-modal dataset containing 100 million high-quality image-text pairs curated from Common Crawl.\nL17: To ensure superior data quality, we develop an effective systematic pipeline comprising data source selection, text refinement, visual diversification, and cross-modal cross-batch filtering, thereby effectively mitigating the intrinsic noise prevalent in web data. Notably, DanQing incorporates data from 2024-2025, enabling models to capture contemporary semantic trends and emerging concepts.\nL18: Extensive experiments via continued pretraining of SigLIP2 models demonstrate that DanQing consistently outperforms existing Chinese datasets across diverse downstream tasks, including zero-shot classification, cross-modal retrieval, and Chinese-centric large multimodal model tasks. Furthermore, in-depth analysis of DanQing reveals that it exhibits a more balanced semantic distribution and superior scaling capability compared to existing datasets.\nL19: To facilitate further research in Chinese vision-language pre-training, we will open-source the DanQing dataset under the Creative Common CC-BY-NC 4.0 license.\nL20: Comments:  | 19 pages, 11 figures, 7 tables\nL21: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV); Artificial Intelligence (cs.AI)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite21†arXiv:2601.10305 [cs.CV]\nL23:    | (or cite22†arXiv:2601.10305v3 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL24:    | cite23†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2601.10305†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Kaicheng Yang [cite24†view email ]\nL28: cite5†[v1] Thu, 15 Jan 2026 11:28:58 UTC (16,992 KB)\nL29: cite25†[v2] Fri, 30 Jan 2026 09:10:07 UTC (16,578 KB)\nL30: [v3] Wed, 25 Mar 2026 05:19:11 UTC (16,578 KB)\nL31: \nL32: Full-text links:\nL33: \nL34: ## Access Paper:\nL35: \nL36: View a PDF of the paper titled DanQing: An Up-to-Date Large-Scale Chinese Vision-Language Pre-training Dataset, by Hengyu Shen and 12 other authors\nL37: \nL38:   * cite19†View PDF L39:   * cite20†HTML (experimental) L40:   * cite26†TeX Source L41: \nL42: cite27†view license†creativecommons.org L43: ### Current browse context:\nL44: \nL45: cs.CV\nL46: \nL47: cite28†< prev |   cite29†next > L48: \nL49: cite30†new | cite31†recent | cite32†2026-01 L50: \nL51: Change to browse by:\nL52: \nL53: cite33†cs L54: cite34†cs.AI L55: \nL56: ### References & Citations\nL57: \nL58:   * cite35†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L59:   * cite36†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L60:   * cite37†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L61: \nL62: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL63: \nL64: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL65: \nL66: [Button: ×]\nL67: \nL68: loading...\nL69: \nL70: Data provided by:\nL71: \nL72: ### Bookmark\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL75: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL76: \nL77: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL78: \nL79: Bibliographic Explorer (cite38†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL80: \nL81: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL